Because x is now const, the compiler has a guarantee that x can’t be changed after initialization. This makes it more likely the compiler will apply constant propagation, and then optimize the variable out entirely.Key insightUsing const variables can help the compiler optimize more effectively.Optimization can make programs harder to debug
